**LOAN AGREEMENT**

**January 14, 2021**

**1. AGREEMENT**

1.1 This Loan Agreement (the "Agreement") is entered into as of the date first written above between WESTERN EQUITIES INC., a Delaware corporation, its subsidiaries, and affiliates (collectively, the "Lender"), and ABC CORP., a Delaware corporation, and XYZ, LTD, an English company (collectively, the "Borrowers").

1.2 The Lender and the Borrowers may be referred to herein individually as a "Party" and collectively as the "Parties."

**2. LOAN TERMS**

2.1 The Lender has agreed to lend to the Borrowers the principal amount of Twenty Million United States Dollars (USD $20,000,000) (the "Loan Amount"), subject to the terms and conditions set forth herein.

2.2 The Loan Amount shall be made available to the Borrowers in one or more advances on the dates specified in Section 3 (the "Advance Dates").

**3. INTEREST AND FEES**

3.1 The Borrowers shall pay interest on the outstanding principal balance at a rate of 5% per annum (the "Interest Rate").

3.2 The Interest Rate shall be calculated on the basis of a 360-day year.

3.3 Interest shall be paid on the Advance Dates and shall accrue from the date of each advance until the date of payment.

3.4 The Borrowers shall also pay all fees, expenses, and charges incurred in connection with the Loan, including without limitation, legal fees, document preparation costs, and appraisal fees (the "Fees").

**4. DEFAULT AND REMEDIES**

4.1 If the Borrowers fail to make any payment when due, or commit any other default under this Agreement, the Lender may declare all amounts owing under this Agreement immediately due and payable, without prejudice to any other rights or remedies available to the Lender at law or in equity.

4.2 The Lender may exercise any rights or remedies provided by applicable law, including without limitation, foreclosure, repossession, and the right to offset any amounts owing by the Borrowers to the Lender against any assets held by the Lender.

**5. MISCELLANEOUS**

5.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Delaware, without giving effect to its conflict of law principles.

5.2 Any notices required or permitted under this Agreement shall be in writing and shall be delivered by personal delivery, registered or certified mail, or nationally recognized overnight delivery service.

**6. SIGNATURES**

In witness whereof, the Parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.

